From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - don't expect the ICV in an authenc decryption response

An authenc decryption sends the ICV at the end of the data. The SPU
checks it and returns the plaintext, the computed digest and the
status, without the ICV. handle_aead_req() expects the ICV in the
response data, so the receive table is one digest too long:

- Out of place, dst has no room for an ICV, and the request fails:

    alg: aead: authenc-hmac-sha1-cbc-aes-iproc decryption failed on
    test vector 0; expected_error=0, actual_error=-14, cfg="out-of-place"

- In place, the status lands in the digest buffer, and the status
  buffer reads as success. A message with a bad ICV then decrypts
  without an error.

Leave the ICV out of the response length of every decryption, as GCM
and CCM already do. Broadcom's own driver for this SPU, in the
BCM47622 SDK, does the same.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -1311,6 +1311,7 @@ static int handle_aead_req(struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx)
 	int err;
 	unsigned int chunksize;
 	unsigned int datalen;
+	unsigned int resp_len;
 	u32 spu_hdr_len;
 	u32 db_size;
 	u32 stat_pad_len;
@@ -1382,12 +1383,15 @@ static int handle_aead_req(struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx)
 
 	incl_icv = spu_req_incl_icv(ctx->cipher.mode, rctx->is_encrypt);
 	datalen = chunksize;
-	if (incl_icv) {
+	if (incl_icv)
+		datalen -= digestsize;
+	resp_len = chunksize;
+	if (!rctx->is_encrypt) {
 		/*
 		 * Input is ciphertxt plus ICV, but ICV not incl
 		 * in output.
 		 */
-		datalen -= digestsize;
+		resp_len -= digestsize;
 	}
 
 	/*
@@ -1397,7 +1401,7 @@ static int handle_aead_req(struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx)
 	 * to dst sg when processing response.
 	 */
 	rctx->src_nents = spu_sg_count(rctx->src_sg, rctx->src_skip, datalen);
-	rctx->dst_nents = spu_sg_count(rctx->dst_sg, rctx->dst_skip, datalen);
+	rctx->dst_nents = spu_sg_count(rctx->dst_sg, rctx->dst_skip, resp_len);
 	if (aead_parms.assoc_size)
 		assoc_nents = spu_sg_count(rctx->assoc, 0,
 					   aead_parms.assoc_size);
@@ -1535,7 +1539,7 @@ static int handle_aead_req(struct iproc_reqctx_s *rctx)
 
 	err = spu_aead_rx_sg_create(mssg, req, rctx, rx_frag_num,
 				    aead_parms.assoc_size,
-				    aead_parms.ret_iv_len, datalen, digestsize,
+				    aead_parms.ret_iv_len, resp_len, digestsize,
 				    stat_pad_len);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
